9. Falsifiable Predictions

The proposed experiment generates several specific, falsifiable predictions. Failure to meet these criteria would constitute evidence against the MGWU hypothesis.

1. Structural Superiority (Multi‑Geometric vs. Unified): Model B will outperform Model A* (the structured single‑space baseline) on compositional generalization on CLEVRER by a statistically significant margin, demonstrating that explicit geometric separation provides benefits beyond mere architectural inductive bias. We will pre‑register the effect size threshold based on a power analysis using the Causal‑JEPA baseline as a reference.
2. Causal Necessity: Model C will outperform Model B on counterfactual questions involving causal chains of 3 or more events, demonstrating that an explicit causal geometry provides a distinct advantage over a purely observational multi‑geometric model. Causal‑JEPA will serve as an additional baseline for this comparison.
3. Metacognitive Routing: Model D will achieve a significantly higher routing accuracy (i.e., the self‑model selects the correct geometry for each query) than a random baseline, and this will translate into improved overall performance and better calibration (lower ECE) compared to Model C.
4. Selective Impairment: Ablating the causal geometry from a trained Model C (by zeroing out its contribution) will lead to a greater degradation in performance on causal chain questions than on simple prediction questions, demonstrating selective functional specialization.
5. Causal Identifiability: In the toy environment, the learned causal graph will match the true causal graph with high probability, consistent with the identifiability guarantees from CRL theory [Lee, Jin & Aragam, 2026].
6. Efficiency Gain: On a Pareto frontier (accuracy vs. training FLOPs), the multi‑geometric models will dominate the single‑space baselines, indicating that structured representation yields better sample and compute efficiency during training. We will also report inference cost to show whether this advantage persists at deployment time.

